From c5831a89bcb92be2add0b6bc2eb11cff063431e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?St=C3=A9phane=20Graber?= <stgraber@stgraber.org>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 20:08:07 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] incusd: Refuse dates the database can't read back
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Expiry and creation dates supplied by clients, directly or through an
image's metadata or a snapshots.expiry, were stored as given. A year
past 9999 is written with five digits but can't be parsed on read, so
every listing touching the row failed and the expiry tasks stopped.

This addresses GHSA-v855-hxm9-5pwg (CVE pending)

Signed-off-by: Stéphane Graber <stgraber@stgraber.org>
(cherry picked from commit 39811b554001078d2f19252f21f9bbdca9b79aba)
---
